The Windows native JARs retain the registration-only native binaries used in the
accepted benchmark. The JavaCPP native JAR has been repackaged to omit Microsoft
runtime DLLs (and unused LLVM OpenMP); only its original jnijavacpp.dll is retained.
Microsoft's runtime is a separately installed Windows prerequisite, not a component
redistributed under RIPR's licence. The remaining JARs are not general-purpose
OpenCV/OpenBLAS packages. OpenCV third-party licence texts accompany this bundle;
their inclusion does not claim that every listed component is present in it.
OpenCV's Enhanced Correlation Coefficient optimizer and phase correlation are
upstream components, not methods invented by RIPR.
